# Step 10 — Shared Tool Gateway Implementation

## 1. Objective

Implement a centralized, secure and reusable Shared Tool Gateway in the existing GeFlow backend.

The Shared Tool Gateway will provide a controlled interface through which authorized GeFlow agents and approved backend components can request access to permitted business operations.

Instead of allowing individual agents to connect directly to databases, APIs or internal business modules, the gateway will act as the central enforcement point for tool discovery, authorization, validation, execution and auditing.

The gateway must support the future integration of all 29 specialized agents while preserving:

- Agent identity.
- Organization isolation.
- Business-level access restrictions.
- Category-level permissions.
- Resource ownership validation.
- Agent-specific capability restrictions.
- Existing GeFlow business logic.
- Human approval requirements for sensitive operations.

**Core architectural principle: One shared gateway, independently enforced permissions for every agent, organization, category and operation.**

