## 10. Tool discovery and retrieval

Implement controlled tool discovery.

Authorized callers should be able to retrieve:

- Available tools.
- Tool descriptions.
- Tool input schemas.
- Tool output schemas.
- Tool versions.
- Required permissions.
- Tool status.
- Approval requirements.

Discovery must be filtered according to the caller's authorized agent, organization, category and capability context.

### Restrictions

- Do not reveal tools the agent is not permitted to use.
- Do not expose internal secrets or credentials.
- Do not reveal unrestricted database access capabilities.
- Do not allow callers to register new tools through ordinary discovery endpoints.
- Do not expose inactive or deprecated tools as executable.

Tool discovery does not grant execution permission.

The gateway must independently revalidate all permissions during invocation.

