## 18. Testing requirements

### 18.1 Tool registry tests

- Register an approved tool.
- Retrieve a registered tool.
- Validate tool schema.
- Reject duplicate tool IDs.
- Reject invalid versions.
- Reject invalid lifecycle transitions.
- Reject unauthorized tool modifications.

### 18.2 Tool discovery tests

- Authorized agent sees permitted tools.
- Unauthorized agent cannot discover restricted tools.
- Inactive tools cannot be presented as executable.
- Discovery does not grant execution access.

### 18.3 Invocation tests

- Valid read operation succeeds.
- Valid authorized write operation succeeds.
- Invalid input is rejected.
- Unknown tool is rejected.
- Inactive tool is rejected.
- Incompatible agent version is rejected.
- Unauthorized agent is rejected.
- Unauthorized organization is rejected.
- Unauthorized category is rejected.
- Resource ownership violation is rejected.

### 18.4 Approval tests

- Approval-required operation enters pending state.
- Rejected operation does not execute.
- Approved operation executes only after revalidation.
- Unauthorized approver is rejected.
- Modified request cannot reuse an earlier approval.
- Expired approval cannot authorize execution.

### 18.5 Reliability tests

- Timeout handling.
- Duplicate request handling.
- Idempotent write handling.
- Concurrent execution controls.
- Safe failure behavior.
- Partial transaction rollback where supported.

### 18.6 Regression tests

Verify existing GeFlow modules continue to function:

- Authentication.
- Organization access.
- Category authorization.
- Agent Registry.
- Agent versioning.
- Products.
- Inventory.
- POS and billing.
- Purchases.
- Suppliers.
- Customers.
- Reports.
- Existing APIs.

